:: StoryTitle
The Ninefold Cell: the duel, step 3 (`define`)

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "<generated by Twine>",
  "format": "Inkjot",
  "format-version": "0.6.0",
  "start": "sanctum"
}

:: Inklink [config]
(((
Step 3 of `define` (docs/define.md): the archetypes of step 2 become words
of their own. `spell ember_lance: …` in place of `combo ember_lance: … ~
like spell`. Only what differs from step 2 (`ex2-duel-step2-fields.twee`)
is here.

What step 3 adds:

| Word | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `:: spell [define combo]` | `spell` is a new declaration word, and a spell is a combo |
| `act self: …` / `combo self: …` below `--` | The clauses every one of them gets |
| `"defined_as": "spell"` in the IR | So the platform can show a spellbook |

Found while writing it: Roland's spells are not one general kind. Five are
combos of cantrips; `lodestone` is a single act. A defined word builds on
one kind, so either there are two words (`spell` and `word`, below) or
`lodestone` becomes a combo of one act it does not have. Step 1's `like
spell` covers both, because an archetype is a tag, not a kind.
)))

steel strike ~ when hask.grounded and me.holds.any(sword)
steel guard
steel raise ~ when me.holds.lumen
steel shatter ~ loud ~ at mirror here ~ when target.open
steel smash ~ loud ~ when me.holds.heart

:: cantrip [define act]
verb: speak
--
act self: cost 10

:: spell [define combo]
verb: cast
field school: fire, frost, sound, time
--
combo self: for roland

:: word [define act]
verb: speak
field school: fire, frost, sound, time
--
act self: for roland

:: steel [define act]
--
act self: cost 20 ~ for eldric ~ when not me.frozen

:: hex [define threat]
verb: casts
field school: fire, frost, light, none ~ default none
field hit: text ~ default ""
field block: text ~ default ""
field deflect: text ~ default ""
field fail: text ~ default ""
--

:: roland [character]
state rewound: no
--
cantrip spark: "a snap of heat and light at a point you can see"
cantrip chill: "frost on a surface, or a mouthful of water turned to ice"
cantrip gust: "one breath of wind, enough to snuff a candle across a room"
cantrip mend: "knits a small break: a torn page, a cracked pin, a split lip"
cantrip tug: "an unseen pull on something lighter than a book, within sight"
cantrip hush: "swallows one sound for a moment" ~ quiet

spell ember_lance: spark, gust, spark ~ school fire ~ "flame, fanned, then lit into a lance"
~ at character here ~ when target.frozen
~ then set target.frozen: no
spell rime_shield: chill, mend, chill ~ school frost ~ "a shell of ice that heals its own cracks"
~ at character here
~ then cover target
spell frostglass: chill, gust ~ school frost ~ "rimes a mirror over until it shows nothing"
~ at mirror here ~ when target.open
~ then set target.open: no
spell thunderclap: hush, gust, spark ~ school sound ~ loud ~ "a swallowed sound, carried, then let go at once"
~ then prevent hask when hask.rhyme.next.school in [fire, frost]
spell backward_knot: mend, hush, tug, mend ~ school time ~ "ties the hour back on itself"
~ rewind ~ once per turn ~ requires pov.all alive

word lodestone: "makes one thing very, very heavy, for one breath"
~ cost 30 ~ school time ~ learned from lodestone ~ when roland.knows.lodestone
~ at npc here
~ then set target.grounded: yes
~ then pin target

:: hask_duel [npc]
--
stat wards: 3
stat wards: 2 when heart.cracked

pattern rhyme: flame, frost, blink, sunfall ~ repeat ~ one per round
~ recall first when hask.saw_heart and holder != nobody and not heart.cracked
~ falter instead of sunfall when holder != nobody and not heart.cracked

hex flame ~ school fire ~ at roland ~ answered by prevent, block, cover, absorb
~ then wound target 1
~ hit "Fire takes Roland full in the chest."
~ block "Eldric takes the fire meant for Roland on his own chest, and staggers, and stays up."
~ deflect "Eldric turns the flame aside on Abelard’s blade, and it splashes harmless across the floor."
hex frost ~ school frost ~ at eldric ~ answered by prevent, cover, absorb
~ then kill target when target.frozen
~ then set target.frozen: yes
~ hit "Ice climbs Eldric to the shoulders and holds him fast."
hex blink ~ fails when count(mirror, in: here, open: yes) == 0 or hask.pinned
~ then set hask.dodging: yes
~ then set hask.grounded: yes next round
~ on fail: set hask.grounded: yes
~ hit "He steps into a mirror and out of the other, and lands on his feet, laughing."
~ fail "He throws himself at the glass and hits frost, hard. He lands on the flagstones in a heap of robes."
hex sunfall ~ school light ~ at pov.all ~ answered by cover, absorb
~ then kill target
~ hit "Light, all of it, everywhere at once."
hex recall ~ at holder ~ answered by block, cover, absorb
~ then take heart
~ hit "The heart leaps from your hand to his, like a dog called home."
hex falter
~ hit "Nothing. He will not burn his own heart, and he knows you know it."
